well let's take you to bristol now where  police and protesters have been clashing  following a demonstration against plans  to give police new powers to restrict  protests as you can see here things have  turned  violent as dark has fallen outside  bridewell  police station in the city center  thousands had gathered  earlier in the day defying current  covert restrictions before marching to  this police station  they've been graffitiing the side of the  building and police say  that missiles including a firework have  been thrown at them  and a number of police vehicles have  been set on fire  and attacked as you can see there we've  also been hearing reports that some  police officers have suffered suspected  broken bones in the last few moments  we've had a statement from avon and  somerset police they say they are  dealing with  a significant disorder in the city  center they say following a protest held  earlier today  several hundred people congregated  outside bridewell police station  during the afternoon chief  superintendent will white  the gold commander has said what started  out as a peaceful protest  has been turned by a small minority into  a violent disorder  he says these scenes are absolutely  disgraceful  and they will be widely condemned by  police across the city  they can never be any excuse for wanton  disorder  officers have been subjected to  considerable levels of abuse and  violence  one suffered a broken arm and another  suffered broken ribs  both have been taken to hospital these  are men and women  out there with the intention of serving  and protecting the public  they should never be subjected to  assaults or abuse in this way  at least two police vehicles have been  set on fire  and damage has been caused to the  outside of the station protesters are  not  inside the building let's bring in our  correspondent dan whitehead who joins us  there  uh live from bristol dan really truly  shocking scenes the kind of violence  that hasn't been seen on the streets of  bristol for  well dare i say decades yeah many years  indeed and there's no sign of this uh  protest ending any time  soon i'm stood i would say around about  30 meters away  from where the police found was on fire  you may would have seen the images  of that police van it said on fire that  the fire is now out but there are still  a number of protesters um on top of part  of bridewell police station which is in  the center of bristol there are  mounted police at the front of this  illegal demonstration i would estimate  that there are around  800 to around a thousand protesters  still  here um and plenty of police officers in  full riot here  i'm actually stood right next to a  police van which is covered completely  in graffiti it's light smashed at the  back  and a whole row of police officers with  riot shields  some of which have been sprayed with  graffiti  and words against the police all over  their actual  riot shield these police still holding a  line  i did for a moment go up to the front of  the  protest where the mounted police are  right by the  police station very lively uh atmosphere  up there a lot of music being played  clearly a lot of people who've been  drinking uh this is of course an illegal  demonstration that's gone on throughout  the day  and as that evening has gone on people  the tone of the protest has clearly  changed but this is very serious there's  a lot of smashed glass everywhere  fireworks have been set up in the street  but you can see the smoke rising in  front of bridewell police station  where that police van that was on fire  that is now  just about under control but clearly a  very serious situation which has  resulted in police officers being  injured smashed windows at the police  station and clearly  a situation which is far from over at  the  moment
 

